Your interview prep brief: rebuild a broken hiring system.
The scenario. Your new team hires slowly, the loop has six rounds of unstructured chats, debriefs never say no, new hires take four months to contribute, and your best engineer is quietly interviewing elsewhere.
Deliverables.
- A redesigned loop: signal per round, no redundancy, structured questions with rubrics.
- A debrief format that can say no: evidence-based, with a written decision record.
- A 30/60/90 onboarding plan for the next hire: buddy, early wins, clarity per phase.
- A retention plan for the at-risk engineer: growth, recognition, work — with a timeline.
- A five-minute spoken case for the hiring bar: why it is the highest-leverage system you own.
Grading lens. Hiring rounds score systems thinking: is there signal per round, can the debrief reject, is ramp speed designed — and is retention proactive?

